let's bring in the nation's doctor  Surgeon General dr. Jerome Adams one of  our favorite people in public service  could you sir explain to us the virus  and some of the unknowns because it  feels like we learn a little bit more  every day about how it might be  transmitted well Dana thank you for  having me and I want to be straight with  the American people I want them to know  that this virus is a new situation that  is changing we're learning about it each  and every day but I do want America to  know that the risk right now is is low  to the average American we know there  are higher risk groups we know that if  you are older if you have medical  comorbidities such as diabetes heart  disease or lung disease you are at  higher risk but I want to give you some  perspective really quickly 18,000 people  have died of the flu in this country  this year so far and as you mentioned at  the top 11 people have died from corona  virus and while our hearts go out to  each and every family who's lost an  individual it's an important that we  keep things in perspective and we  recognize that we can do things to keep  our country safe we have a list of the  tips to prevent it they're the ones  we've been hearing about you avoid being  around people that are sick avoid  touching eyes nose and mouth and you  stay home and you know wash your hands  frequently and then there's also these  recommendations from the CDC about a  face mask  I loved your tweet the other day what do  you think about face masks well it's  important for folks to know that face  masks are not recommended for the  general public there there are two  things people should know number one if  you wear a face mask and you're not  wearing it properly you're going to be  more likely to touch your face and you  can actually increase your risk of  getting a respiratory disease like  corona virus or flu number two when  people hoard masks they are not  available for health care providers who  actually need them so my advice to folks  stop buying masks if you're part of the  general public leave them for the  healthcare provider so they can take  care of people who are sick I was  reading about a couple of universities  out on the west coast suggesting that  their students not travel out of the  country for their Spring Break  you know everybody likes to go and have  a big party they're encouraging them to  stay in the United States is that  something you think is a good idea well  I I don't know that we're quite  there yet but I think that every  institution every state needs to be  thinking about this I just got off the  phone with the governor of Ohio we  talked with the governor of Connecticut  earlier this week and the vice president  and I were in Florida talking to the  governor there last week we want people  to review their preparedness plans we  want them to think about what their  triggers should be because what folks  need to remember is these decisions are  made at the state and local level not at  the federal level and they're going to  be different in Seattle you you may do  different things in terms of closures  than what you would do on Ohio or  Connecticut right now but we've been  here before  MERS SARS h1n1 we have preparedness  plans and now's the time for people to  execute those preparedness plans and  make sure they're making the right  decisions for the people in their states  and communities I have two last  questions for you one of them is that  because there are going there's going to  be more testing we will likely see the  number of cases for people testing  positive go up but that's that isn't any  reason for people to panic is that right  exactly we expect to see more cases  unfortunately we will likely see more  deaths but again many more people will  likely die from the flu in this country  this year and then we'll even get sick  from coronavirus and we want folks to do  the things that they can do to control  spread of disease another important  thing is for people to get their flu  shot because when hospitals are  overflowing with flu patients they won't  be able to take care of people who have  corona virus and so again there are  things you can do to stay safe wearing a  mask is not one of them my last question  for you is just any advice you have for  those of us in the media who want to  cover the story responsibly to get  information out to people but also do  not make them overly concerned or not  undersell it either do you have any  advice for us what exactly we don't want  to undersell this this is a serious  global health threat but we want people  to keep it in perspective we want them  to know we've been here before we want  them to know we have the best team in  the world  Tony Falchi and sugar Robert Redfield  ambassador birx working to keep them  safe 24/7 and if we do the things that  we prepared to do preparedness over  panic facts over fear and go to CDC gov  for regular updates then I'm confident  we can get through this  you're a terrific Surgeon General  dr. jerome adams we love having you  thank you for giving us some of your  time thanks Dana did you get your flu  shot this year absolutely
 

